@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Database & Tables Introduction";
}

<section>

    <!-- PAGE INTRODUCTION -->
    <div class="mb-5">

        <h1 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Database & Tables Introduction
        </h1>

        <p class="lead text-muted">
            A database is used to store and organize data, while tables
            are used to store data in rows and columns. In SQL Server,
            databases and tables form the foundation for storing and
            managing structured information.
        </p>

    </div>


    <!-- WHAT IS A DATABASE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            What is a Database?
        </h2>

        <p>
            A database is a structured collection of information that
            allows data to be stored, managed and retrieved efficiently.
        </p>

        <p>
            In SQL Server, a database can contain tables, views,
            stored procedures, functions and other database objects.
        </p>

        <div class="alert alert-primary border-0">

            <h5 class="fw-bold">
                Example
            </h5>

            <p class="mb-0">
                A college application may have a database named
                <strong>CollegeDB</strong> that stores student,
                course and teacher information.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- DATABASE STRUCTURE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Database Structure
        </h2>

        <p>
            A SQL Server database can contain multiple database objects.
            A simple structure can be represented as follows:
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL Server
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>
                                                        Database
                                                           ↓
                                                        Tables
                                                           ↓
                                                        Rows & Columns
                                                           ↓
                                                         Data</code></pre>

        </div>

        <p>
            Tables are one of the most important objects inside a
            database because they store the actual data.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- WHAT IS A TABLE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            What is a Table?
        </h2>

        <p>
            A table is a database object used to store related information
            in the form of rows and columns.
        </p>

        <p>
            Each column represents a specific type of information, while
            each row represents one complete record.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- ROWS AND COLUMNS -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Rows and Columns
        </h2>

        <p>
            Consider a <strong>Students</strong> table:
        </p>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>StudentId</th>
                        <th>StudentName</th>
                        <th>Age</th>
                        <th>Course</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td>1</td>
                        <td>Rahul</td>
                        <td>22</td>
                        <td>Java</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>2</td>
                        <td>Priya</td>
                        <td>21</td>
                        <td>.NET</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>3</td>
                        <td>Amit</td>
                        <td>23</td>
                        <td>Python</td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

        <ul>

            <li class="mb-2">
                <strong>Column:</strong> Defines the type of information
                stored.
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                <strong>Row:</strong> Represents one complete record.
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                <strong>Table:</strong> Collection of related records.
            </li>

        </ul>

    </section>


    <!-- DATABASE AND TABLE RELATIONSHIP -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Database and Table Relationship
        </h2>

        <p>
            A database can contain multiple tables. Each table can store
            data related to a particular entity.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL Server
            </div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>
                                                        CollegeDB
                                                           │
                                                           ├── Students
                                                           │
                                                           ├── Courses
                                                           │
                                                           ├── Teachers
                                                           │
                                                           └── Departments</code></pre>

        </div>

        <p>
            For example, the <strong>Students</strong> table stores
            student information, while the <strong>Courses</strong>
            table stores course information.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- CREATING A DATABASE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Creating a Database
        </h2>

        <p>
            The <strong>CREATE DATABASE</strong> statement is used to
            create a new database in SQL Server.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE DATABASE CollegeDB;</code></pre>

        </div>

        <p>
            After executing this statement, SQL Server creates a new
            database named <strong>CollegeDB</strong>.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- CREATING A TABLE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Creating a Table
        </h2>

        <p>
            The <strong>CREATE TABLE</strong> statement is used to create
            a table inside a database.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE TABLE Students
(
    StudentId INT,
    StudentName VARCHAR(100),
    Age INT,
    Course VARCHAR(50)
);</code></pre>

        </div>

        <p>
            This statement creates a table named
            <strong>Students</strong> with four columns.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- COMMON DATABASE OPERATIONS -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Common Database & Table Operations
        </h2>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>Operation</th>
                        <th>SQL Statement</th>
                        <th>Purpose</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Create Database</td>
                        <td>CREATE DATABASE</td>
                        <td>Create a new database.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Create Table</td>
                        <td>CREATE TABLE</td>
                        <td>Create a new table.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Alter Table</td>
                        <td>ALTER TABLE</td>
                        <td>Modify table structure.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Drop Table</td>
                        <td>DROP TABLE</td>
                        <td>Remove a table.</td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- IMPORTANT -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <div class="alert alert-warning border-0">

            <h5 class="fw-bold">
                Important
            </h5>

            <p class="mb-0">
                A database contains database objects, and tables are
                primarily used to store structured data in rows and
                columns. Choosing a proper table structure is important
                for managing data efficiently.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- SUMMARY -->
    <section class="mb-4">

        <div class="alert alert-primary border-0">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Summary
            </h2>

            <p class="mb-0">
                In this section, we learned what a database and table are,
                how databases and tables are organized, the difference
                between rows and columns, and the basic SQL statements
                used to create databases and tables.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


